# Drafted by Gemini (R15 side_wedding), edited.

~ thibault_start
Narrator: Black water laps over the porch planks, soaking the hem of the minister's cassock while she wrings out a soggy prayer book.
odalys_thibault [weary]: Mind the second step, the catfish nested under it again. I am supposed to marry Marguerite and Ignatius before high tide, and nothing in this parish is ready.
* What is needed? -> thibault_need
* We will help -> thibault_accept
* Not now -> END

~ thibault_need
odalys_thibault [weary]: Luckless Lou pawned the wedding band to cover a wager on a one-legged heron. Beyond that, we have no fiddler for the aisle and no supper for the table.
interject name:delphine_ravelle: A wedding with no ring, no fiddle, and no supper? Darling, that is just a puddle.
-> thibault_start

~ thibault_accept
odalys_thibault [neutral]: Bless your dry boots. Speak with Lou, Tibby, and Mama Pelletier, and come back before the pews float off their blocks.
set wedding_asked
quest a_wedding_at_the_mud_church asked
-> END

~ thibault_progress
Narrator: The Reverend shakes her pocket watch, watching a tiny minnow swim past the Roman numerals.
odalys_thibault [weary]: The water is up to the altar rail and the groom is still breathing into a paper sack. Tell me we have something to show the bride.
* [if flag.wedding_score >= 1] Begin the wedding with what we have -> ceremony
* Ask what is done -> thibault_status
* [ends:a_wedding_at_the_mud_church] Call the wedding off -> call_off
* Leave -> END

~ thibault_status
odalys_thibault [neutral]: Let us see what grace has spared us between the mud and the mosquitoes.
if flag.wedding_ring
odalys_thibault [smile]: We have the brass ring back from the pawn ledger, which is one miracle.
endif
if flag.wedding_music
odalys_thibault [smile]: There is music waiting on the porch, even if the fiddler is leaning against a post.
endif
if flag.wedding_supper
odalys_thibault [smile]: Mama Pelletier sent word that the big kettle is coming down the boardwalk.
endif
-> thibault_progress

~ ceremony
approve delphine_ravelle +3 tobin_hayward +2 rook_coldwake +2: You saw the mud-church wedding through before high tide
set wedding_outcome = "held"
quest a_wedding_at_the_mud_church done
Narrator: Lantern light trembles on the black water between the pews as Marguerite and Ignatius join hands above the flood.
interject name:lucan_houndstooth: Damp ankles or no, they stand proud at the rail. Lovely.
if flag.wedding_score >= 3
odalys_thibault [smile]: With a ring, a tune, and hot gumbo waiting on the dock, I have never seen a finer wedding in six inches of swamp.
gold +80
else
odalys_thibault [smile]: It was short on trimmings and wet around the ankles, yet they are lawfully wed and smiling through the damp.
gold +30
endif
-> END

~ call_off
approve delphine_ravelle -3 tobin_hayward -2 rook_coldwake -2: You called off Marguerite and Ignatius's wedding
set wedding_outcome = "off"
quest a_wedding_at_the_mud_church lost
Narrator: The Reverend sits down on the step, the bride and groom go their separate ways, and the water comes up another inch.
odalys_thibault [sad]: Perhaps we will try again when the river goes down, though I have been saying that since last autumn.
-> END

~ lou_ring
luckless_lou [sly]: Look, the heron had a terrible limp and four-to-one odds, so pawning Ignatius's ring was practically an investment. I still hold the ticket right here in my vest.
* [Persuasion DC 13] Talk him into giving the pawn ticket up -> lou_ring_ok | lou_ring_no
* [if gold >= 5] Buy the pawn ticket for five gold -> lou_ring_paid
* Leave -> END

~ lou_ring_ok
set wedding_ring
set wedding_score += 1
Narrator: Lou lets out a long breath that smells of cheap rye and hands over the crumpled pasteboard stub.
luckless_lou [weary]: Take it, then, before you make me feel like a churchwarden. A man cannot even back a bird in peace.
-> END

~ lou_ring_no
luckless_lou [smile]: Friends, I operate on a strict mathematical system, and charity prior to the third race ruins the whole arithmetic.
-> lou_ring

~ lou_ring_paid
gold -5
set wedding_ring
set wedding_score += 1
luckless_lou [smile]: Five gold covers the bird, the ticket, and my bruised pride. Give the bride my warm regards.
-> END

~ music
tibby_marsh [smile]: You need a fiddler before the tide turns? Old Ches is sleeping under a skiff by the eel pens, and I know which plank to kick.
* [if gold >= 2] Pay Tibby two gold for a fiddler -> music_pay
* [Performance DC 12] Play something ourselves -> music_play | music_miss
* Leave -> END

~ music_pay
gold -2
set wedding_music
set wedding_score += 1
Narrator: Tibby is gone and back before the coin stops spinning, towing a fiddler who is asleep on his feet.
tibby_marsh [smile]: Prop him against the doorframe and poke his ribs when the bride walks in. He knows three reels and a hymn.
-> END

~ music_play
set wedding_music
set wedding_score += 1
tibby_marsh [smile]: Well, that beats the bullfrogs hollow. The Reverend says just keep playing that until everyone sits down.
-> END

~ music_miss
Narrator: A sour note skitters across the dark lagoon, and a one-legged heron on the piling turns to look at {name}.
tibby_marsh [sly]: My aunt had a dying billy goat that made that exact noise. Maybe try again once your fingers warm up.
-> music

~ supper
mama_pelletier [neutral]: A wedding without a hot pot is just two damp people arguing in front of a preacher. My crawfish gumbo is thick enough to stand a spoon in.
* [if flag.gumbo_tasted] Ask her to cook the supper -> supper_yes
* Taste the gumbo first -> supper_taste
* [if gold >= 15] Pay fifteen gold for it -> supper_paid
* Leave -> END

~ supper_yes
set wedding_supper
set wedding_score += 1
mama_pelletier [smile]: Since you know good roux when it hits your tongue, I will haul the iron kettle over to the church porch myself.
-> END

~ supper_taste
mama_pelletier [sly]: Take a ladle from the simmering pot by my elbow before we talk business. I do not cook for strangers who eat with their eyes shut.
-> END

~ supper_paid
gold -15
set wedding_supper
set wedding_score += 1
mama_pelletier [smile]: Fifteen gold buys the whole kettle, six loaves of tallow bread, and my promise to keep Lou out of the gravy.
-> END

~ bride
marguerite_salt [neutral]: Ignatius will show up once his boots stop shaking, so do not fret over him. Tell me instead if anyone has seen my cousin Odell down by the boathouse.
-> END

~ groom
Narrator: Ignatius sits on the wet church step in his good leather boots, staring down at the minnows around his heels.
ignatius_fontaine [afraid]: I love Marguerite more than dry land, truly I do. It is just that every good thing in Murkwater Bend goes bad the moment you put your name to it.
* [Persuasion DC 12] Steady him -> groom_ok | groom_miss
* Sit with him a while -> groom_ok
* Leave -> END

~ groom_ok
Narrator: He nods, gets up, sits down again, and gets up, squaring his shoulders against the damp night air.
ignatius_fontaine [smile]: You are right, the water is rising whether I stand at that altar or not. Best to meet it beside a sensible woman.
-> END

~ groom_miss
ignatius_fontaine [weary]: My head knows every word you are saying, friend, but my feet have taken root in this porch.
-> groom

~ bell
Narrator: You tug the rope on the cracked ship's bell, which rings a flat iron note that shivers the porch and brings dark water welling up through the planks.
-> END
